General Steps:\par
1. Installation: Download and install VS Code for your OS from the official site.\par
2. Configuration for Web Development: Recommended extensions: Live Server, Prettier, ESLint, and built-in HTML/CSS/JS support.\par
(A screenshot of VS Code with HTML/CSS/JS and extensions installed would be placed here.)\par
----------------------------------------\par\par
\b 8. Static vs. Dynamic Websites\b0\par
Static Website:\tab Content is pre-built and stored as fixed HTML files. Limited interactivity; same content for all users. Technologies: HTML, CSS, client-side JS.\par
Dynamic Website:\tab Content is generated on the fly when a user requests the page. Uses backend languages and databases; highly interactive and personalized content.\par
Examples:\par
	ab Static: Personal portfolio or corporate brochure site.\par
	ab Dynamic: Social networks, e-commerce sites, news websites.\par
----------------------------------------\par\par
\b 9. Five Web Browsers and Rendering Engines\b0\par
Google Chrome \tab - Blink\par
Mozilla Firefox \tab - Gecko / Quantum\par
Apple Safari \tab - WebKit\par
Microsoft Edge \tab - Blink\par
Opera \tab - Blink\par
How Rendering Engines Differ: Implementation details, performance characteristics, and standards support vary; modern engines have improved cross-browser consistency.\par
